      "pointer": "/records/2/procedure",
      "before": "SOUL PYRE — NEW RD8-PYRE-02; explicitly8d6 total, split4d6 fire plus4d6 necrotic.\nACCESS / CAST: Cleric, Druid or Wizard with actual rank-8 Necromancy access, minimum class level15; Action, base21RP, V/S and the actual M/F alternative. No priced reagent is invented. A reusable focus can satisfy the focus alternative but cannot supply the real corpse that fuels the effect. Instantaneous; no continuing concentration outside a held Ready.\nCORPSE / OWNERSHIP: Select one actually perceived, physically present principal corpse/remains body record, whose genuine death and origin are recorded and which is currently available and not already consumed or disallowed as a resource by its own source. NEW eligibility completion: one retained principal body identity is the unit, regardless of size, prior creature type or age; a severed part, pile assembled from fragments or duplicate reference is not another principal body. Ordinary missing-part history or skeletal principal remains does not alone prohibit it. No minimum body mass, percentage, humanoid-only, necromancy-only or arbitrary age cutoff is added. There must actually be one qualifying principal corpse now; unresolved global decay cannot be assumed to supply one. A Dying0/Stable0 living body is not eligible. No phantom body, copied form, already-consumed standard animated body or expired/destroyed finite summon supplies new fuel. A genuine Ranger beast corpse or a genuinely reconstructed body later dying can qualify only through its own actual current body history and permissions; no owner-level/CR test applies. This spell needs no consent from a deceased body's former controller, but neither transfers legal ownership of surviving gear nor asserts ownership/finality of any soul.\nGEOMETRY: NEW separation of the two20-foot values: the corpse's fixed current body-origin/anchor must be within20 feet of the caster source, with genuine perception and line of effect. On effect resolution its actual current anchor is the center of a20-foot-radius closed3D sphere. Select all actual creatures with body intersection and center-to-the-same-witness line of effect, including the caster, allies and carrier. No favorable exclusions, objects or structural damage are implied. Real corpse inventory survives as described below. An actual acquired initial-area exclusion, such as the Wizard's Evocation-only benefit, applies only if its exact prerequisites hold; Soul Pyre is Necromancy and gains no Evocation permission by analogy.\nATOMIC FUEL TRANSACTION: NEW spell-specific choice: the corpse is selected but neither reserved nor consumed during commitment or its counter window. At resolution revalidate that same identity at its actual current anchor, still within range/LoE, source-eligible and available. A move that still satisfies all predicates moves the eventual blast center; an out-of-range move, prior consumption, actual return to life or other invalidation prevents the paid effect without a substitute or refund. Resolve simultaneous consumers in the established neutral authoritative event order. At the valid effect checkpoint atomically claim and mark this one body consumed, snapshot blast geometry/recipients and create the blast event. No later consumer can claim its old corpse; a previously provisional Auto-Raise reservation confers no priority over actual lawful consumption. A countered spell consumes no corpse. For Ready the actual corpse is selected/rechecked at release; there is no preparation-time corpse lock. This is not a global change to printed consumed spell materials.\nDAMAGE: Each admitted creature makes a DEX save. One shared raw pool of four d6 fire and four d6 necrotic serves this blast. Failure takes each full type; success halves each type with floor before RD8-MIXED-02 and actual defenses. Separate recipient roots share the original caster as dealer, not the dead body's former owner. It remains one original-recipient event per creature, with source-qualified transfers, temp HP, life and concentration. Absence, immunity or suppression at a recipient does not refund consumed fuel or give a second blast. If the creating manifestation itself is wholly prevented at the fuel/source checkpoint, consumption does not begin. Zero admitted damage recipients still leaves a lawfully executed corpse-burning effect, but creates no unnecessary damage RNG or roots.\nREMAINS / END: NEW physical completion: burn the principal body into spent ordinary ash/char at its actual location, retaining the same consumed-body lineage and missing-part/corpse history. Never create a second corpse/fuel/loot entitlement by splitting ashes. Surviving worn, carried or lodged real items are not consumed or automatically damaged by the spell; detach them locally at their actual positions under ordinary support/fall rules, preserving IDs and provenance. No remote deposit or inventory deletion. Actual non-damage material consumption is not converted by Null. Later dispel cannot restore the corpse or refund costs. A separate reconstruction/resurrection source must independently support these actual spent remains, its costs and restrictions; this spell grants neither such a recovery nor a metaphysical ban on it. Soul Pyre supplies no soul capture, RP, healing or resource-return rider.",
      "after": "SOUL PYRE — NEW RD8-PYRE-02; explicitly8d6 total, split4d6 fire plus4d6 necrotic.\nACCESS / CAST: Cleric, Druid or Wizard with actual rank-8 Necromancy access, minimum class level15; Action, base21RP, V/S and the actual M/F alternative. No priced reagent is invented. A reusable focus can satisfy the focus alternative but cannot supply the real corpse that fuels the effect. Instantaneous; no continuing concentration outside a held Ready.\nCORPSE / OWNERSHIP: Select one actually perceived, physically present principal corpse/remains body record, whose genuine death and origin are recorded and which is currently available and not already consumed or disallowed as a resource by its own source. NEW eligibility completion: one retained principal body identity is the unit, regardless of size, prior creature type or age; a severed part, pile assembled from fragments or duplicate reference is not another principal body. Ordinary missing-part history or skeletal principal remains does not alone prohibit it. No minimum body mass, percentage, humanoid-only, necromancy-only or arbitrary age cutoff is added. There must actually be one qualifying principal corpse now; unresolved global decay cannot be assumed to supply one. A Dying0/Stable0 living body is not eligible. No phantom body, copied form, already-consumed standard animated body or expired/destroyed finite summon supplies new fuel. A genuine Ranger beast corpse or a genuinely reconstructed body later dying can qualify only through its own actual current body history and permissions; no owner-level/CR test applies. This spell needs no consent from a deceased body's former controller, but neither transfers legal ownership of surviving gear nor asserts ownership/finality of any soul.\nGEOMETRY: NEW separation of the two20-foot values: the corpse's fixed current body-origin/anchor must be within20 feet of the caster source, with genuine perception and line of effect. On effect resolution its actual current anchor is the center of a20-foot-radius closed3D sphere. Select all actual creatures with body intersection and center-to-the-same-witness line of effect, including the caster, allies and carrier. No favorable exclusions, objects or structural damage are implied. Real corpse inventory survives as described below. An actual acquired initial-area exclusion, such as the Wizard's Evocation-only benefit, applies only if its exact prerequisites hold; Soul Pyre is Necromancy and gains no Evocation permission by analogy.\nATOMIC FUEL TRANSACTION: NEW spell-specific choice: the corpse is selected but neither reserved nor consumed during commitment or its counter window. At resolution revalidate that same identity at its actual current anchor, still within range/LoE, source-eligible and available. A move that still satisfies all predicates moves the eventual blast center; an out-of-range move, prior consumption, actual return to life or other invalidation prevents the paid effect without a substitute or refund. Resolve simultaneous consumers in the established neutral authoritative event order. At the valid effect checkpoint atomically claim and mark this one body consumed, snapshot blast geometry/recipients and create the blast event. No later consumer can claim its old corpse; a previously provisional Auto-Raise reservation confers no priority over actual lawful consumption. A countered spell consumes no corpse. For Ready the actual corpse is selected/rechecked at release; there is no preparation-time corpse lock. This is not a global change to printed consumed spell materials.\nDAMAGE: Each admitted creature makes a DEX save. One shared raw pool of four d6 fire and four d6 necrotic serves this blast. Failure takes each full type; success halves each type with floor before RD8-MIXED-02 and actual defenses. Separate recipient roots share the original caster as dealer, not the dead body's former owner. It remains one original-recipient event per creature, with source-qualified transfers, temp HP, life and concentration. Absence, immunity or suppression at a recipient does not refund consumed fuel or give a second blast. If the creating manifestation itself is wholly prevented at the fuel/source checkpoint, consumption does not begin. Zero admitted damage recipients still leaves a lawfully executed corpse-burning effect, but creates no unnecessary damage RNG or roots.\nREADY SELF-DAMAGE / CREATED BLAST — NEW RD8-PYRE-READY-BATCH-03, only for Soul Pyre: ordinary Ready concentration continues through this instantaneous resolution. Loss of that concentration before the valid fuel-consumption/blast-creation checkpoint prevents creating the blast and consumes no corpse; already paid preparation costs remain spent. Once that checkpoint has actually consumed the fuel, frozen the recipients and created their roots, resolve the already-created instantaneous blast once in the scene's fixed recipient order. If its own damage reaches the concentrating caster, make the actual CON concentration save immediately after that damage/life processing, before continuing to later recipients: DC max(10, floor(resolved event damage/2)), with the caster's actual modifiers and features. Success retains the hold until end-of-resolution cleanup. Failure ends the hold immediately, without delaying unrelated concentration/life consequences, but does not unconsume the corpse, cancel or resample the already-created instantaneous blast, erase completed damage or create another root/roll/payment. A later recipient still uses its actual current existence and defenses. At completion clear any surviving hold once; a hold already ended by failure is not ended or released a second time. This is a new Soul-Pyre-only completion of its existing atomic blast transaction, not a global Ready or all-instantaneous-spells exception, and it changes neither Incendiary Cloud's nor the Wall's separately named batch rule.\nREMAINS / END: NEW physical completion: burn the principal body into spent ordinary ash/char at its actual location, retaining the same consumed-body lineage and missing-part/corpse history. Never create a second corpse/fuel/loot entitlement by splitting ashes. Surviving worn, carried or lodged real items are not consumed or automatically damaged by the spell; detach them locally at their actual positions under ordinary support/fall rules, preserving IDs and provenance. No remote deposit or inventory deletion. Actual non-damage material consumption is not converted by Null. Later dispel cannot restore the corpse or refund costs. A separate reconstruction/resurrection source must independently support these actual spent remains, its costs and restrictions; this spell grants neither such a recovery nor a metaphysical ban on it. Soul Pyre supplies no soul capture, RP, healing or resource-return rider."
